 'calloutsMicroGlued':[['What you see','A sectioned sample of hardened cement paste: globular hydration products, air pores, plate-shaped and needle-shaped crystals, two broken aggregate grains. The crack runs through it with fine branches. Nothing is drilled: the component stays untouched.'],['Through the adhesive packers','The packers are bonded over the crack on the surface with {EKF}. The resin enters the crack from there at low pressure and runs along it into the depth of the component.'],['{P4}: the seal','The honey yellow resin has a low viscosity (approx. 125 mPa·s at 20 °C), so it also reaches the fine branches. It adheres to the flanks and cures to soft elastic: the permanent, crack-bridging seal. Adhesive packers need a dry or damp crack that does not conduct water.']],
 'calloutsMicro':[['What you see','A sectioned sample of hardened cement paste: globular hydration products, air pores, plate-shaped and needle-shaped crystals, two broken aggregate grains. The {defect} runs through it with fine branches. The section follows the axis of the drilled hole, so the hole shows as a half pipe that meets the {defect} at 45°.'],['{P1}: first injection','Only where the {defect} conducts water. The dark brown resin runs along the hole into the {defect}, reacts with the water and foams to up to 40 times its volume. The watertight, visco-plastic foam stops the ingress of water. It is a temporary seal.'],['{P4}: second injection','The honey yellow resin has a low viscosity (approx. 125 mPa·s at 20 °C), so it also reaches the fine branches that the foam does not fill. It adheres to the flanks and cures to soft elastic: the permanent, crack-bridging seal. Afterwards the packer is removed and the hole plugged with {M30}.']],'m3d.xray':'X-ray view','m3d.reset':'Reset view','m3d.hint':'Drag to rotate · Shift + drag to pan',
