    'rc.m3d.xray': 'X-ray view', 'rc.m3d.reset': 'Reset view', 'rc.m3d.zin': 'Zoom in', 'rc.m3d.zout': 'Zoom out', 'rc.tl.prev': 'Previous steps', 'rc.tl.next': 'Next steps', 'rc.m3d.hint': 'Drag to rotate · Shift + drag to move · Ctrl + wheel to zoom', 'rc.m3d.aria': 'Interactive 3D model of the crystalline waterproofing build-up',
    'rc.sec.aria': '3D section through the waterproofed component, stage by stage', 'rc.sec.hint': 'Section through the component · drag to rotate', 'rc.hero.hint': 'Drag to rotate · select a step', 'rc.hero.aria': '3D sample panel of the crystalline waterproofing system: the six steps of the build-up side by side',
    'rc.m3d.microNote': 'Micro scale: schematic close-up of a sectioned sample at the coating interface, not to scale. Each stage plays as a short animation.', 'rc.m3d.microBuild': 'Building the micro-scale model …',
    'rc.m3d.microSub': { rctank: 'Micro scale shows the interface itself: the pores and a fine crack of the concrete skin, the two coats of {IC} on it, and the crystals growing from the coating into the pores and the crack until the water standing on the finished tank can no longer enter.', rcwall: 'Micro scale shows the jetted concrete skin, water pressing into the pores and the crack from the rear, the two coats of {IC} — and the crystals that grow into the capillaries and the crack and hold the water back (negative side, up to 1.5 bar).', rcpit: 'Micro scale shows the concrete skin of the pit with water pressing from the rear, the two coats of {IC}, and the crystals filling the capillaries and the crack until the pit stays dry.', rcsew: 'Micro scale shows the concrete skin of the tank, the two coats of {IC}, and the crystals growing into the pores and the crack — the sealed pore structure keeps the aggressive water out of the concrete.' },
    'rc.m3d.co': { rctank: [['Made good before it is coated', 'Water jetting at > 400 bar lays the concrete bare; static cracks over 0.4 mm are chased 20 × 25 mm, their edges screened with {IC} and filled flush with {IM}; the coved fillet of approx. 4 cm follows wet in wet.'], ['Two coats into the damp concrete', '{IC} is brushed evenly into the repeatedly wetted, matt damp substrate; the second coat while the first is still sticky; 1.5 kg/m² for accumulated water. It can be sprayed (Technical Information No. 43).'], ['Kept damp, then filled', 'Protected from sun and wind for ≥ 24 hours, kept damp for ≥ 3 days from the day after application; filling possible after 3 days, drinking water tanks rinsed first. Pressurised water after ≥ 7 days; up to a month to the full sealing effect.']],
      rcwall: [['Stop the water first', 'Where water runs through the joint the opening is chiselled to a dovetail and a plug of {F20} is pressed in by hand until it hardens — after 1–2 minutes, with a noticeable warming, even under water.'], ['Chased, filled, coved', 'The construction joint and the cracks are chased 20 × 25 mm, screened with {IC} and filled flush with {IM}; the coved fillet of approx. 4 cm on a screen of {IC}; {IC} over the fresh mortar after 1–3 hours.'], ['Two coats against the pressure', '{IC} in two coats into the matt damp concrete, 1.5 kg/m² for pressing water: the crystals grow into the capillaries and hold negative pressing water up to 1.5 bar. Kept damp ≥ 3 days, ventilated, no condensation.']],
      rcpit: [['Relieve, then plug', 'Under high water pressure a hose is set into a chiselled depression at the strongest flow and fixed with {F20}: the pressure is relieved while the joint around it is plugged. After drying the hose is removed and its hole plugged.'], ['Cove and cracks with ASOCRET-IM', 'The wall–floor joint receives a coved fillet of {IM} of approx. 4 cm on a screen of {IC}; holes and chased cracks are filled flush, up to 10 mm per step.'], ['Sealed and ventilated', 'Two coats of {IC} over walls and floor into the matt damp concrete; kept damp ≥ 3 days; deep pits are ventilated for 24 hours and the dew point avoided with dryers, never with direct heating.']],
      rcsew: [['Analyse the water', 'Aggressive or soft water (hardness < 30 mg CaO per litre) always requires a water analysis; the degree of attack is evaluated in accordance with EN 1992-1-1. Sludge and biofilm are jetted off; cracks are chased and filled with {IM}.'], ['Two coats, condensation controlled', '{IC} in two coats into the matt damp concrete, 1.5 kg/m² for accumulated water; in containers the dew point is avoided with condensation dryers — direct heating or blowing warm air is not permitted.'], ['Cured, then commissioned', 'Kept damp for ≥ 3 days at a constant relative humidity > 80 %; in service water tanks at 10–15 °C seven days are generally sufficient. Filling after 3 days; the slurry cannot be overcoated with tiles, plaster or paint.']] },
